abstract: "QueryDiff transfers object-level relative structure from a frozen visual teacher to the final prediction queries of an aerial detector. Absolute object anchoring constrains individual fitting errors, while local vector differences couple neighboring query errors within teacher patches. Energy-repeatability weights allocate the difference supervision. Teacher networks and distillation projections are used during training; inference uses the detector alone."
keywords:
  - aerial object detection
  - knowledge distillation
  - remote sensing
  - query-based object detection
